# ── Waitlist storage ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The API picks a backend in this order: Supabase → Neon → local file.
# Set the ones you want and leave the rest blank.

# 1) Supabase (recommended — see docs/waitlist-supabase.md)
#    Project Settings → API. Use the service_role key (server-only, NOT anon).
SUPABASE_URL=
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=

# 2) Neon / Postgres (used only if the Supabase vars are empty)
# WAITLIST_DATABASE_URL=postgresql://user:pass@host/db?sslmode=require

# If none are set, dev writes to a local .data/waitlist.json file.

# ── Rate limiting (optional) ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Salt for hashing IPs before they're used as rate-limit keys, so raw IPs never
# reach the database. Set any long random string in production; a default is used
# if this is blank. Changing it resets all in-flight rate-limit windows.
# RATE_LIMIT_SALT=
#
# With the Supabase vars above set, the limiter uses Postgres and holds across
# instances — run supabase/rate-limit.sql once first. Otherwise it falls back to
# an in-memory counter, which is per-instance (fine for dev).

# ── Analytics (optional) ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Events no-op unless a provider (Plausible / PostHog) is present on the page.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_PLAUSIBLE_DOMAIN=yami.ng
